1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:02,802
Beacon. Brake.

2
00:00:07,238 --> 00:00:12,708
Three buoy gates. One place to stop.

3
00:00:13,808 --> 00:00:19,358
Go through every gate in order.

4
00:00:20,338 --> 00:00:25,708
Finish inside the box, facing forward,
below 0.38 metres per second.

5
00:00:29,978 --> 00:00:35,358
A promising start, if the harbor is behind him.

6
00:00:36,678 --> 00:00:43,227
Gate one is clear. Gate two is less forgiving.

7
00:00:44,175 --> 00:00:49,375
The red mark is where the run ended.

8
00:00:50,095 --> 00:00:56,818
One more turn. He starts it a little late.

9
00:00:57,678 --> 00:01:05,302
All the gates. Still too far left or right,
and the berth will catch him.

10
00:01:06,358 --> 00:01:11,858
From the bow, this looks almost wide enough.

11
00:01:12,858 --> 00:01:17,438
He gets farther in, but can't hold the centreline.

12
00:01:20,508 --> 00:01:25,408
The trainer runs 24 boats in parallel.
Each one tries its own controls.

13
00:01:26,108 --> 00:01:30,808
Each path is a completed training run.
We're playing their combined time at 400×.

14
00:01:34,458 --> 00:01:39,408
The routes start reaching the far side.

15
00:01:48,558 --> 00:01:53,408
Plenty of runs clear the gates.
The boat still has to stop.

16
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:02,550
That one missed the berth and kept going.

17
00:02:28,967 --> 00:02:33,267
The box is almost behind him.

18
00:02:36,533 --> 00:02:41,233
For testing, I saved the same 48 starts.
Here's one before any training.

19
00:02:41,843 --> 00:02:46,133
The throttle barely moves. The current does the rest.

20
00:02:47,157 --> 00:02:52,217
Same start. Same current. Now look at that first turn.

21
00:02:53,917 --> 00:02:58,217
The strongest paths light up. Teal adds. Amber subtracts.

22
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:02,200
We get the view from the bow.

23
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:06,000
Beacon gets 13 numbers, including
where the next gate is and how fast he's moving.

24
00:03:06,830 --> 00:03:11,480
Once the gates are clear, the target changes to the berth.

25
00:03:14,370 --> 00:03:18,950
Watch the wake shrink as he eases off.

26
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:26,450
The current is pushing left on this run.

27
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:33,750
New starting position. Current the other way.

28
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:41,150
Straighten up. Now let the speed come down.

29
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:48,200
Two starts, two different lines into the same berth.

30
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:55,070
The final gate is still a speed run.
The berth is where that approach stops working.

31
00:03:55,890 --> 00:04:01,450
Ease off early enough to straighten up
before the bow reaches the box.

32
00:04:02,770 --> 00:04:08,170
Position, heading, and speed must all hold
for half a second.

33
00:04:34,683 --> 00:04:38,883
At the final checkpoint, all 48 starts get in cleanly.

34
00:04:40,833 --> 00:04:45,133
The first docking took 604 attempts.
Doing it reliably took a little longer.

35
00:04:48,033 --> 00:04:52,283
Good parking, Beacon.
